      "html": "<h1>Computational Decision Science (CDS-410)</h1><h2>Course Description</h2><p>Application of computation, probability, optimization, and behavioral modeling to decision-making under uncertainty.</p><h2>Learning Objectives</h2><ul style=\"list-style-type: none\"><li>• Build probabilistic decision models</li><li>• Apply Bayesian reasoning</li><li>• Solve optimization problems</li><li>• Evaluate decision quality under uncertainty</li></ul><h2>Weekly Topics</h2><p>Week 1: Rational Decision Making Week 2: Utility Theory Week 3: Probability Review Week 4: Bayesian Inference Week 5: Markov Decision Processes Week 6: Multi-Criteria Decisions Week 7: Midterm Week 8: Optimization Methods Week 9: Risk Analysis Week 10: Game Theory Week 11: AI-Assisted Decision Systems Week 12: Capstone Presentations</p><h2>Assessments</h2><p>Quizzes: 15% Midterm: 25% Research Report: 20% Capstone Project: 40%</p><h2>Prerequisites</h2><p>Linear Algebra, Finite Probability, Introductory Programming</p>",
